			},
			"date": "2022-11-21T20:22:06.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> It's me, explaining your projects to myself again! You'll never escape!</p><p>This creates a linkable archive of your Twitter presence, the idea of which is to canonize THOSE links as the \"correct\" links for your tweets going forward. So if you have a lot of content in a blog, like Zach does, that links to tweets, this replaces Twitter as a dependency for that data.</p><p>Is that right?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
