		{
			"id": "109397253035604933",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@addyosmani/109397252940242695",
			"author": {
				"name": "Addy Osmani",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@addyosmani",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/300/741/065/131/572/original/1bbdc3b0a6ae791e.png"
			},
			"date": "2022-11-24T06:00:06.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mamot.fr/@nhoizey\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>nhoizey</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> This was my favorite thing to use this week. Thank you! 🤩 Was really impressed with how well it worked (across 25K tweets). </p><p>My only feedback was uncertainty navigating beyond Recent/Popular/tweet URL seemed a gap. Perhaps by design, but otherwise lookups by tweet URL worked flawlessly 💜</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109397312531980556",
			"parentId": "109397253035604933",
			"url": "https://mamot.fr/@nhoizey/109397312481848042",
			"author": {
				"name": "Nicolas Hoizey",
				"url": "https://mamot.fr/@nhoizey",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/288/230/453/300/889/original/b21203c65dbd197c.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2022-11-24T06:15:15.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@addyosmani\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>addyosmani</span></a></span> great!<br>There’s an issue already open for monthly archives navigation: <a href=\"https://github.com/tweetback/tweetback/issues/15\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">github.com/tweetback/tweetback</span><span class=\"invisible\">/issues/15</span></a></p><p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109397379312676037",
			"parentId": "109397312531980556",
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@addyosmani/109397379277867365",
			"author": {
				"name": "Addy Osmani",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@addyosmani",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/300/741/065/131/572/original/1bbdc3b0a6ae791e.png"
			},
			"date": "2022-11-24T06:32:14.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mamot.fr/@nhoizey\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>nhoizey</span></a></span> Amazing! That’s exactly what I was looking for! <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109397485926143394",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://hachyderm.io/@ro14nd/109397485789473116",
			"author": {
				"name": "Roland Huß 🌶 🇺🇦",
				"url": "https://hachyderm.io/@ro14nd",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2022-11-24T06:59:19.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mamot.fr/@nhoizey\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>nhoizey</span></a></span> wow, that's great! Thanks a lot.</p><p>🤔 wouldn't it be a cool 🎄  vacation project to add a build script that creates a fully running OCI container image with one's tweet archive for ease of sharing without hosting it ? </p><p>Indeed, so I added it to my list 🙂</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109397517629268356",
			"parentId": "109397485926143394",
			"url": "https://mamot.fr/@nhoizey/109397517577059718",
			"author": {
				"name": "Nicolas Hoizey",
				"url": "https://mamot.fr/@nhoizey",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/288/230/453/300/889/original/b21203c65dbd197c.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2022-11-24T07:07:24.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://hachyderm.io/@ro14nd\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>ro14nd</span></a></span> sorry, but what is an \"OCI container image\"? 😅</p><p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109397588314030402",
			"parentId": "109397517629268356",
			"url": "https://hachyderm.io/@ro14nd/109397587955468593",
			"author": {
				"name": "Roland Huß 🌶 🇺🇦",
				"url": "https://hachyderm.io/@ro14nd",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2022-11-24T07:25:18.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mamot.fr/@nhoizey\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>nhoizey</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> OCI formerly known as Docker ;-)</p><p>OCI (Open Container Initiative) is the standard for defining container images that you can run with Docker or other runtimes (containerd, podman,...)</p><p>The benefit here would be, if you have stored your public tweets in such a container, you then could just use something like</p><p>  docker run -p 8080:8080 rhuss/tweets</p><p>And then point your browser to http://localhost:8080 Or run it in a Kubernetes cluster. Or whatever :-)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109397673994670928",
			"parentId": "109397588314030402",
			"url": "https://mamot.fr/@nhoizey/109397673943110607",
			"author": {
				"name": "Nicolas Hoizey",
				"url": "https://mamot.fr/@nhoizey",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/288/230/453/300/889/original/b21203c65dbd197c.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2022-11-24T07:47:10.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://hachyderm.io/@ro14nd\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>ro14nd</span></a></span> oh, I didn’t know about this, thanks.</p><p>You can already run `npm start` if you want to browse you <a href=\"https://mamot.fr/tags/tweetback\" class=\"mention hashtag\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">#<span>tweetback</span></a> archive without sharing it. Isn’t that enough?</p><p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109397841800108252",
			"parentId": "109397673994670928",
			"url": "https://hachyderm.io/@ro14nd/109397841740247535",
			"author": {
				"name": "Roland Huß 🌶 🇺🇦",
				"url": "https://hachyderm.io/@ro14nd",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2022-11-24T08:29:51.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mamot.fr/@nhoizey\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>nhoizey</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> true, but then you need Node installed and fetch all dependencies. And git. Things might break in the future (left-pad anyone? :-). </p><p>OCI containers are fully self contained and contain all those dependencies within the image.You can run it anytime in the future anywhere without rebuilding or checking dependencies. Not so bad for an archive ;-)</p><p>Let me do a quick prototype to make it more clear what I mean. Will send you a PR.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109397854700029034",
			"parentId": "109397841800108252",
			"url": "https://mamot.fr/@nhoizey/109397854621114540",
			"author": {
				"name": "Nicolas Hoizey",
				"url": "https://mamot.fr/@nhoizey",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/288/230/453/300/889/original/b21203c65dbd197c.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2022-11-24T08:33:07.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://hachyderm.io/@ro14nd\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>ro14nd</span></a></span> ok, it makes sense. 👍</p><p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109398249996204834",
			"parentId": "109397854700029034",
			"url": "https://hachyderm.io/@ro14nd/109398249939090743",
			"author": {
				"name": "Roland Huß 🌶 🇺🇦",
				"url": "https://hachyderm.io/@ro14nd",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2022-11-24T10:13:39.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mamot.fr/@nhoizey\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>nhoizey</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Here's a first prototype --&gt; <a href=\"https://github.com/tweetback/tweetback/pull/26\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">github.com/tweetback/tweetback</span><span class=\"invisible\">/pull/26</span></a> </p><p>You can try it out with my tweets by running `docker run -p 8080:8080 rhuss/tweets`</p><p>Thanks a lot for creating and open sourcing this package, this is very helpful for us immigrants ;-)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109398330347621833",
			"parentId": "109398249996204834",
			"url": "https://mamot.fr/@nhoizey/109398330300032580",
			"author": {
				"name": "Nicolas Hoizey",
